{'symbol': 'RL', 'date': '2020-05-27 10:30:00', 'title': 'RALPH LAUREN REPORTS Q4 REVENUE $1.3 BLN', 'text': 'RALPH LAUREN REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER AND FULL YEAR FISCAL 2020 RESULTS.Q4 REVENUE $1.3 BILLION.QTRLY LOSS PER SHARE $3.38.QTRLY ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE $0.68.NORTH AMERICA REVENUE IN Q4 DECREASED 11% TO $629 MILLION.INVENTORY AT END OF FISCAL 2020 WAS $736 MILLION, DOWN 10% COMPARED TO THE PRIOR YEAR PERIOD.ASIA REVENUE IN Q4 DECREASED 22% TO $214 MILLION ON A REPORTED BASIS AND DECREASED 21% IN CONSTANT CURRENCY.RALPH LAUREN - STRENGTHENED BALANCE SHEET, NEAR-TERM LIQUIDITY WITH OVER $2 BILLION IN CASH & INVESTMENTS, KEY EXPENSE REDUCTION ACTIONS.HAVE REOPENED ABOUT TWO THIRDS OF STORES IN EUROPE AND NEARLY HALF OF STORES IN NORTH AMERICA THROUGH LAST HALF OF MAY.RALPH LAUREN - EUROPE REVENUE IN Q4 DECREASED 19% TO $353 MILLION ON REPORTED BASIS, DECREASED 16% TO LAST YEAR IN CONSTANT CURRENCY.DUE TO HIGH LEVEL OF UNCERTAINTY AND EVOLVING SITUATION SURROUNDING COVID-19, SUSPENDING ALL FUTURE GUIDANCE.EXPECT RESULTS FOR FY21 AND Q1 TO BE SIGNIFICANTLY NEGATIVELY IMPACTED BY THE PANDEMIC.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $-0.40, REVENUE VIEW $1.22 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.RALPH LAUREN - IN RETAIL, QTRLY COMPARABLE STORE SALES IN N.AMERICA WERE DOWN 13%, INCLUDING 15% DOWN IN BRICK & MORTAR STORES & 7% DOWN IN DIGITAL COMMERCE.ASIA REVENUE IN Q4 DECREASED DUE TO IMPACTS FROM COVID-19 AND HONG KONG PROTEST BUSINESS DISRUPTIONS.'}